{"slug":"/allie-tsubota","title":"Allie Tsubota","kicker":"","section":"","hero":{"src":"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/55d61c1be4b0cafd401171f5/938330b2-d672-4a5e-bbb5-abdbbece3c30/5+-+Dead+Letter+Room+%28installation+view%29+-+d7e01b45-f1c5-4d66-95c5-4a002387e093.jpg","w":1500,"h":1000,"fx":0.5,"fy":0.5,"alt":""},"description":"<p><strong>Allie Tsubota</strong></p><p>© Allie Tsubota</p>","seoTitle":"","seoDescription":"PENUMBRA WORKSPACE PROGRAM | FINALIST | 2025 All residents →  Allie Tsubota is an artist exploring intersections of race, visuality, and the formation of historical memory. Her wor","nodes":[{"t":"row","cols":[{"span":10,"nodes":[{"t":"html","html":"<h3>PENUMBRA WORKSPACE PROGRAM | <strong>FINALIST</strong> | 2025</h3>"}]},{"span":2,"nodes":[{"t":"html","html":"<p><a href=\"/workspace-residency-2025\">All residents  →</a></p>"}]}]},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"row","cols":[{"span":6,"nodes":[{"t":"img","src":"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/55d61c1be4b0cafd401171f5/00682395-f67e-4225-b529-0883ca61fcaa/12+-+Dead+Letter+Room+%28USSBS-+Hiroshima%29+-+787a7f20-2c6e-4f3c-b07f-4e6cd5326489.jpg","w":1500,"h":1200,"fx":0.5,"fy":0.5,"alt":"","caption":"<p>Image © Allie Tsubota. Courtesy of the artist.</p>"}]},{"span":6,"nodes":[{"t":"html","html":"<p><strong>Allie Tsubota</strong> is an artist exploring intersections of race, visuality, and the formation of historical memory. Her work joins photography, video, photographic and cinematic archives, and text to examine the role of visual spectatorship across racialized space and collapsed historical time. Tsubota has received recognitions from Aperture, Google’s Creator Lab, The Museum of Contemporary Photography in Chicago, and PhMuseum, among others, and has been an artist-in-residence with Headlands Center for the Arts, the Center for Photography at Woodstock, and ARCUS Project (Japan). Her works have been exhibited across the United States and in Japan. Tsubota holds an MFA in Photography from Rhode Island School of Design, and presently teaches photography at Parsons School of Design and Pratt Institute.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.allietsubota.com/\">allietsubota.com</a></p>"}]}]},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"gallery","layout":"grid","per":6,"images":[{"src":"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/55d61c1be4b0cafd401171f5/1747247116412-U8HJCDQAXDVI1JTPU4OS/11+-+Dead+Letter+Room+%28USSBS-+Hiroshima%29+-+fcab0c30-cd0b-419a-8c4c-3f8d028620a1.jpg","w":1500,"h":1200,"fx":0.5,"fy":0.5,"alt":""},{"src":"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/55d61c1be4b0cafd401171f5/1747247928059-A1SPN8XSY86UXK1U12T1/14+-+Dead+Letter+Room+%28USSBS-+Hiroshima%29+-+dd419071-aac0-4abd-9926-e7bc56277fff.jpg","w":1500,"h":1200,"fx":0.5,"fy":0.5,"alt":""},{"src":"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/55d61c1be4b0cafd401171f5/1747247931728-5FQ90Z5D4CEW9JHC0SHC/8+-+Dead+Letter+Room+%28-Asakusa-%29+-+60866cd2-0df7-40c7-b0cc-5994e44985cb.jpg","w":1500,"h":1200,"fx":0.5,"fy":0.5,"alt":""},{"src":"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/55d61c1be4b0cafd401171f5/1747247938960-8FX3WZ1RE55ELSUQMC61/9+-+Dead+Letter+Room+%28-Yokogawa-%29+-+5cc66247-3ff1-4b81-9df7-417b8ccd33c7.jpg","w":1179,"h":1500,"fx":0.5,"fy":0.5,"alt":""},{"src":"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/55d61c1be4b0cafd401171f5/1747247994026-9842JJB851W8KAA9Y6EI/13+-+Dead+Letter+Room+%28USSBS-+Hiroshima%29+-+045c7436-e51c-4fa5-b205-937f82932f41.jpg","w":1500,"h":1097,"fx":0.5,"fy":0.5,"alt":""},{"src":"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/55d61c1be4b0cafd401171f5/1747248009837-ZUI7ON0P3MFC8Z5T67PW/4+-+Dead+Letter+Room+%28installation+view%29+-+e73f45d2-608d-4e5b-a9a0-736487a5f192.jpg","w":1500,"h":1000,"fx":0.5,"fy":0.5,"alt":""}]},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"html","html":"<h3>SPONSORS</h3><p>This program is sponsored by <strong>Joy of Giving Something </strong>and the <strong>Phillip and Edith Leonian Foundation</strong>.</p>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/55d61c1b